{"term":"peep","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:7ec08fd56483261b98","definition":"A short, soft, high-pitched sound, as made by a baby bird.","example":"I don't want to hear a peep out of you!","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["peepy"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peep#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e17375044981e685a6","definition":"The sound of a steam engine's whistle; typically shrill.","example":"With a \"peep\" from a high-pitched whistle, the train would leave by the crossover to the down line, […].","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["peepy"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peep#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2dcea29d8d0d8f62ac","definition":"A sandpiper or other small wader.","example":"When I spotted two small warm-brown scaley-plumaged ‘peeps’ with yellow legs, my commentary immediately identified them as Least Sandpipers.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"colloquial","register":"colloquial","wordFamily":["peepy"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peep#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b7fa3a6c9fe0b8a7df","definition":"To make a soft, shrill noise like a baby bird.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["peepy","cheep","chirp"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peep#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:85d1bdf7ff96488847","definition":"To speak briefly with a quiet voice.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["peepy","cheep","chirp"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peep#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8e870b985f5ca2a5f1","definition":"To look forth from concealment, especially through a narrow opening, or while trying not to be seen or noticed.","example":"The man peeped through the small hole.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["keek"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["peepy","cheep","chirp"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peep#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2a7a9d2c16e53c5cee","definition":"To begin to appear; to make the first appearance.","example":"When flowers first peeped, and trees did blossoms bear.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"dated","register":"dated, intransitive","wordFamily":["peepy","cheep","chirp"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peep#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:7e05d35407eec90521","definition":"To take a look at; check out.","example":"Did you peep that video I sent you?","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"slang","register":"slang, transitive","wordFamily":["peepy","cheep","chirp"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peep#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:be349351f928e114fe","definition":"To see, uncover.","example":"A lot of females were hesitant about getting with Pimp. He had a hard edge to him that made it impossible not to peep his cruel nature.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"slang","register":"slang, transitive","wordFamily":["peepy","cheep","chirp"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peep#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b68436a3dbf3acc062","definition":"A quick look or glimpse, especially a furtive one.","example":"So saying she loosened some ivory screws of the guitar, so as to open a peep lengthwise through its interior.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["peepy","cheep","chirp","bo-peep","by-peep","day-peep","peek","peep-bo","peep bo","peeper","peepers","peephole","peeping tom","peepless","peepo","peep of day","peep out","peep pixels","peep show","peep sight","peep-toe","pixel peep","pixel peeper","tweep","underpeep","wink-a-peep"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peep#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d1b68c7a075ecef7ee","definition":"The first partial appearance of something; a beginning to appear.","example":"the peep of day","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["peepy","cheep","chirp","bo-peep","by-peep","day-peep","peek","peep-bo","peep bo","peeper","peepers","peephole","peeping tom","peepless","peepo","peep of day","peep out","peep pixels","peep show","peep sight","peep-toe","pixel peep","pixel peeper","tweep","underpeep","wink-a-peep"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peep#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b06d778d18847277f1","definition":"A peepshow.","example":"A boring lusterless attempt at pornography, a niche above the racks of pulp pocketbooks sold in the front room of p